---
layout: base.njk
structuredData: true
title: Communicate with hearing people quickly and easily
description: Deaftly helps deaf people talk with people who can hear. Show a message in big, clear text, use a ready-made template, or chat face to face on one phone.
---
<section class="wrap hero">
<div class="hero__intro">
<h1>Communicate with hearing people quickly and easily</h1>
<p class="lede">Get your message across your way, whatever the moment</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="wrap hero-features" aria-label="What Deaftly does">
<a class="feature-tile" href="/tour/#type-and-show">
<h2>Start typing</h2>
<span>Type anything and show it full screen in big, clear text.</span>
<img class="feature-tile__screen" src="{{ "/screenshots/show.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" alt="">
</a>
<a class="feature-tile" href="/tour/#templates">
<h2>Templates</h2>
<span>Everyday messages, ready to go. Tap the parts that change, or fill them in by reading text live with the camera.</span>
<img class="feature-tile__screen" src="{{ "/screenshots/fill.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" alt="">
</a>
<a class="feature-tile" href="/tour/#face-to-face">
<h2>Face to face</h2>
<span>They read along as you type, while you keep hold of your phone.</span>
<img class="feature-tile__screen" src="{{ "/screenshots/face-to-face.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" alt="">
</a>
<a class="feature-tile" href="/tour/#side-by-side">
<h2>Side by side</h2>
<span>Take turns on one phone, like a script in each person's colour.</span>
<img class="feature-tile__screen" src="{{ "/screenshots/side-by-side.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" alt="">
</a>
</section>

<section class="band" id="features">
<div class="wrap">
<h2>“Can't I just type in my notes app?”</h2>
<p class="lede">A notes app is designed for you to write things down for yourself. Deaftly is for the conversation: making your text easy to hold up and show at a check-in desk; filling in your food order from a menu using your camera; typing to a stranger who doesn't know you're deaf but they can read along right from the first word while you keep a secure grip on your phone; and then continuing into a conversation, with clear prompts for the hearing person, so that you can take turns to type on the same phone.</p>
<p><a class="button" href="/tour/">Take the tour</a></p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="wrap section" id="situations">
<h2>Wherever you need it</h2>
<ul class="situation-grid">
{% for situation in situations %}
<li><a class="situation-card" href="{{ situation.url }}"><strong>{{ situation.title }}</strong><span>{{ situation.summary }}</span></a></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
</section>

{% if quote.approved %}
<section class="wrap section">
<figure class="quote">
<blockquote><p>{{ quote.text }}</p></blockquote>
<figcaption>{{ quote.credit }}</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
{% endif %}

